4. Unexpected one-time cash needs (Medium)
   - Risk: Capex, legal, or supplier disputes can reduce available cash.
   - Mitigation: Maintain a minimum liquidity cushion; require executive approval for >$X expenses; maintain a prioritized cash reserve.

5. Cost creep / hiring and headcount (Medium)
   - Risk: Uncontrolled hiring or fixed-cost commitments raise burn.
