5. Supply chain disruption / inventory build‑up — Ties up cash in inventory or causes missed revenue.
   - Mitigation: Rebalance inventory targets, find alternative suppliers, and renegotiate lead times.
6. Execution risk on cost reduction — Savings targets may be delayed or less than planned.
   - Mitigation: Assign accountable owners, set short deadlines, and track savings monthly.
7. Macroeconomic downturn / demand softness — Reduces revenue and increases discounting pressure.
   - Mitigation: Scenario planning, preserve cash reserves, focus on high‑margin products.
