Executive summary
- Metro Manufacturing enters the board meeting with $2.1M of cash on hand and strong recent topline performance (Q last quarter revenue $1.8M, averaging ~$600K/month). Current reported net burn is $72K/month, which — if accurate as net cash burn — implies ~29 months of runway on current operations. If the company’s internal runway estimate is 20 months, this implies either planned investments or higher forecasted burn going forward; we should confirm assumptions.
- Operationally we are cash-positive on an operating basis relative to runway (revenue >> burn), but growth investments, one-time commitments, or seasonality could materially change the cash trajectory. Key board decisions needed: confirm near-term investment priorities, approve runway extensions (if pursuing just-in-case buffer), and authorize a fundraising plan if we want to increase runway or accelerate growth.

Financial snapshot (bullet metrics)
- Cash: $2.1M
- Reported net burn: $72K / month (confirm definition)
