Board ask: Approve the updated forecast and contingency actions (hiring pause thresholds, discretionary spend limits) and authorize management to begin preparatory fundraising outreach if downside scenarios reduce runway below 12–15 months.

4) Key risks, likelihood/impact (short) and mitigations
- Revenue concentration (High likelihood if a few large customers drive revenue) — Impact: High. Mitigation: Provide % revenue by top 5 customers, accelerate new pipeline, diversify sales focus, negotiate multi‑quarter contracts.
- Receivable / cash collection delays (Medium likelihood) — Impact: Medium–High. Mitigation: Tighten credit terms, offer early‑payment discounts, prioritize collections, review DSO and adjust forecasts.
- Margin compression / rising COGS (Medium) — Impact: Medium. Mitigation: Re‑price where feasible, lock supplier contracts, improve manufacturing efficiency, model worst‑case margin scenarios.
- Cost overruns or hiring commitments (Medium) — Impact: Medium. Mitigation: Freeze nonessential hires, require board approval for incremental >X% cost items, convert fixed to variable where possible.
- Inaccurate runway or forecast assumptions (High) — Impact: High. Mitigation: Reconcile cash/burn/runway now; produce rolling 90‑day cash forecast and weekly cash burn report.
- Macroeconomic / demand slowdown (Medium) — Impact: Medium–High. Mitigation: Scenario planning, reduce discretionary spend, accelerate pipeline conversion activities.
- Supply chain disruption (Low–Medium) — Impact: Medium. Mitigation: Dual sourcing, safety inventory for critical items, update lead‑time assumptions.
- Regulatory/compliance or litigation risk (Low) — Impact: High. Mitigation: Legal review, reserves in forecast, disclosure to board if material.

5) Suggested mitigations & actions to put in the narrative
- Confirm and reconcile runway math and commit to a single canonical forecast (owner: VP Finance; deliverable: updated 12‑ and 24‑month cash model within 5 business days).
- Run base/downside/accelerated scenarios and flag when runway hits 15 and 12 months (triggers for board actions/fundraising).
- Immediate cash preservation: temporary hiring freeze on noncritical roles; pause discretionary marketing spend; review vendor payment terms.
- Revenue protection: prioritize collections, pursue bridge contracts with key customers, and accelerate high‑margin sales channels.
- Fundraising posture: prepare one‑pager and updated financial model for investor outreach if downside scenario reduces runway <12–15 months.

