- Build a short 12‑month cash-flow model under three scenarios (base / downside / upside) once you confirm:
  - whether $72K is net burn or pre-revenue expense,
  - expected revenue growth assumptions (monthly or quarterly), and
  - any planned hires, CapEx, or large contracts in the next 12 months.
- Draft a short talking script (3–4 bullets) for the CEO/Finance lead to present at the board meeting.

Which of the immediate next steps would you like me to do now? If you want the slide/cash model, confirm the burn/runway clarification and any revenue growth assumptions (or I can show standard scenarios: flat revenue, -20% decline, +15% growth).

