  - Start collections push for past-due AR.
- 30–90 days:
  - Implement supplier/payment term negotiations.
  - Run scenario models (base, downside, upside) and produce slide for next board meeting.
  - Begin contingency financing conversations (one lender, one investor) if runway < 18 months under downside.
- 90–180 days:
  - Execute structural cost reductions only if downside scenario materializes.
  - Reassess pricing, product mix, and distribution channels.

5) Suggested KPIs to track weekly / monthly
- Cash balance (actual vs forecast)
- 13-week cash forecast variance
- Monthly net cash burn
- Revenue vs plan (by product/customer)
- Gross margin %
- DSO / AR aging
- Inventory days
- New orders backlog

