Key risks, prioritized (with suggested mitigations)
1) Revenue slowdown or customer churn
- Why it matters: A sudden drop in demand or loss of a large customer could reduce cash inflows and shorten runway quickly.
- Likelihood/impact: Medium / High (if revenue is concentrated)
- Mitigations: diversify customer base, accelerate renewals, add contract terms with upfront payments, tighten collections, run 0/–10/–20% revenue scenarios and stress-test cash.
- Metric to report monthly: revenue QoQ, top 5 customers % of revenue, days sales outstanding (DSO).

2) Receivables and cash conversion (DSO increase)
- Why: Slow collections reduce usable cash even if bookings look good.
- Mitigations: credit limits, stricter payment terms, incentives for early payment, factoring as short-term option.
- Metric: DSO, cash collected vs invoiced.

3) Understated future burn (hiring, projects, capex)
- Why: Planned hires or one-off investments can materially increase burn versus current run-rate.
- Mitigations: require board sign-off for hires above thresholds, stage projects with go/no-go gates, include hiring freeze triggers.
- Metric: monthly actual burn vs plan, committed spend vs forecast.

4) Supply chain or input-cost inflation (margin compression)
- Why: Increased costs can reduce margins and necessitate higher cash outflows.
- Mitigations: renegotiate supplier contracts, pass-through pricing clauses, hedging where appropriate, prioritize higher-margin product lines.
- Metric: gross margin by product, input cost trends.

5) Capital/financing constraints or market timing
- Why: If we decide to raise growth capital and market conditions are poor, the timing/cost of capital could be unfavorable.
- Mitigations: maintain optionality (extend runway via cost flexibility), prepare a near-term bridge plan, line-of-credit or committed debt facility as backup.
- Metric: liquidity runway under downside scenarios, lender/term-sheet readiness.

6) One-time large liabilities / regulatory / warranty claims
- Why: Unexpected liabilities can deplete cash quickly.
- Mitigations: maintain contingency reserve, update insurance coverage, legal review of exposures.
- Metric: contingency reserve, outstanding claims.

7) Concentration risk (customers, suppliers, geographies)
- Mitigations: diversification plans, second-source suppliers, contractual protections.

