I can help — below I’ve prepared a concise board-ready finance summary, a short finance narrative you can read aloud, and a prioritized list of key risks with mitigation actions and KPIs to monitor. Before finalizing slides or an email, one important data check: the numbers you gave are inconsistent (see first section). Please confirm which figures are correct (or tell me how you define “burn rate”) and I’ll adjust the final wording and any recommended asks.

1) Quick data reconciliation (please confirm)
- You provided: Cash = $2.1M; Runway = 20 months; Burn = $72K/month; Revenue last quarter = $1.8M.
- If burn = $72K/month, implied runway = 2.1M / 72K ≈ 29.2 months (not 20 months).
- If runway = 20 months, implied burn = 2.1M / 20 = $105K/month (not $72K).
- Revenue last quarter $1.8M => monthly revenue ≈ $600K; annualized revenue run-rate ≈ $7.2M.
- Clarify: is “burn rate” net cash burn after revenue, or operating cash outflow before revenue? Which number (burn vs runway) should be treated as authoritative?

2) One-page board summary (concise)
- Cash position: $2.1M (as of [date]).
- Revenue: $1.8M last quarter (≈ $600K/month; annualized run-rate ≈ $7.2M).
- Burn / runway (confirming calc): if net burn = $72K/month → runway ≈ 29 months. If runway = 20 months → implied net burn ≈ $105K/month.
- Recent trend: Q[ ] revenue growth/decline vs prior quarter (please supply trend if available). Highlight any material customer wins/losses or timing of large receivables.
- Liquidity outlook: At current stated burn, we have multi-quarter coverage; if burn is higher or revenue weakens, runway compresses — monitoring required.
- Primary near-term objective: Protect runway while accelerating revenue stability and predictable collections.
- Board asks (high level): (1) Approve updated 12-month cash forecast and scenario plan (best/base/worst). (2) Authorize contingency financing trigger (if runway < X months). (3) Support temporary cost-liquidity measures if required (e.g., hiring freeze, defer non-essential capex).

3) Short finance narrative / talking points (1–2 paragraphs)
- Suggested narrative for the board meeting:
  "We finished the quarter with $2.1M in cash and generated $1.8M in revenue last quarter (≈ $600K/month, annualized run-rate ≈ $7.2M). Based on the current metrics you provided, there is sufficient liquidity to operate for multiple quarters without immediate financing. That said, I want to flag a reconciliation item: the stated burn and runway figures don’t align — we will confirm whether the $72K monthly burn is net of revenue or represents operating cash outflows. We are proposing an immediate update to the 12-month cash forecast under best / base / worst-case scenarios, and to set a clear board contingency trigger for raising capital if runway falls below [board-preferred threshold, e.g., 12 months]. Our operational focus for the next quarter is on stabilizing revenue, improving collections, and prioritizing investments that directly increase margin and recurring revenue."

4) Key risks (prioritized) with suggested mitigations
- Liquidity / Financing Risk (High impact)
  - Description: Runway sensitivity to higher-than-expected burn or revenue decline.
  - Mitigation: Finalize monthly cash forecast; set a board-approved trigger (e.g., 12 months) to begin fundraising; prepare investor-ready materials; postpone non-critical spend.
- Revenue Concentration (High)
  - Description: Large customers or a few accounts representing high % of revenue.
  - Mitigation: Report customer concentration metric; diversify pipeline; negotiate longer-term contracts and prepayments.
- Revenue Volatility / Collection Risk (Medium–High)
  - Description: Slower collections or quarter-to-quarter revenue swings compress cash flow.
  - Mitigation: Tighten AR terms, weekly collections dashboard, incentives for earlier payment, reserve for bad debt.
- Cost Overruns / Hiring (Medium)
  - Description: Uncontrolled hiring or recurring costs increase burn.
  - Mitigation: Immediate hiring freeze for non-essential roles; require Finance sign-off for hires and major contracts.
- Market / Demand Downturn (Medium)
  - Description: Macro slowdown causes lower order volume or pricing pressure.
  - Mitigation: Stress-test revenue scenarios; prioritize high-ROI sales initiatives and retention programs.
- Supply Chain / Delivery Risk (Medium)
  - Description: Disruptions increasing COGS or delaying revenue recognition.
  - Mitigation: Identify alternate suppliers, renegotiate terms, hold safety inventory for critical items.
- Execution / Product Risk (Medium)
  - Description: Product delays that impact renewals or renewals churn.
  - Mitigation: Prioritize roadmap items tied to customer retention; transparently communicate timelines to customers.
- Compliance / Legal (Low–Medium)
  - Description: Contract disputes or regulatory fines.
  - Mitigation: Legal review of large contracts, maintain reserve and insurance where appropriate.

5) KPIs and metrics to present monthly to the board
- Cash balance (actual) and 12-month cash forecast by scenario
- Net monthly burn (cash outflows - cash inflows) and trend
- Revenue (monthly & quarterly), M/M and Q/Q growth rates
- Gross margin and contribution margin
- AR days (DSO) and receivables aging
- Customer concentration (% revenue from top 3 customers)
- Sales pipeline value and conversion rate; churn / retention
- Headcount and fixed vs variable cost split
- Capex and near-term committed spend

6) Suggested near-term action plan (next 30–90 days)
- Immediate: Confirm/clean the core numbers (clarify burn definition and reconciling items).
- 7–14 days: Deliver a 12-month cash forecast under three scenarios (best/base/worst) with weekly cash model updates.
- 14–30 days: Present contingency financing plan and investor materials (if board approves).
- 30–90 days: Implement cost controls, accelerate collections, and focus sales initiatives to protect revenue run-rate.

7) Suggested asks for the board (concise)
- Approve updated 12-month forecast and scenario planning.
- Approve a runway trigger and contingency fundraising plan.
- Support temporary cost control measures / hiring pause until forecast stabilizes.

8) Next steps I can help with right now
- If you confirm which numbers are authoritative (burn vs runway) I will:
  - Produce a one-slide board finance summary (text ready for the deck) and a 1-page appendix with the three-scenario cash model outline.
  - Draft a short email to the board summarizing the finance position and the meeting ask.
  - Or produce CFO talking points tailored to the board meeting (2–3 bullets per topic).
  
Which would you like me to prepare next? And please confirm whether the $72K burn or the 20-month runway is correct (and whether burn is net of revenue).

